    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 102043\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1243 PM PST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Quiet and pleasant conditions anticipated through Friday morning.\n\n* Cooler conditions and a chance of showers returns late Friday\n  into Saturday, with a stronger system poised to affect the\n  region early next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through next Tuesday.\n\nExpect a few more days of pleasant weather before a change in the \npattern arrives this weekend. High pressure over the region \nmaintains dry conditions and above normal temperatures for this time \nof year. Breezy northerly winds pick up in the afternoon today and \ntomorrow in the Colorado River Valley as high pressure builds to \nthe north and creates a strong north to south pressure gradient. \n\nA series of incoming disturbances will influence regional weather \nstarting Friday. The first feature is a closed low that will move\ninland south of the U.S.-Mexico border on Friday. The low is too \nfar to the south to send substantial moisture into the forecast \narea by itself. However, it will be followed closely by a stronger\nshortwave trough that will traverse the Great Basin Friday night \ninto Saturday and phase with the low over Mexico. This setup \nshould support moisture advection inland from the west and \nsouthwest, a direction that will mainly affect the Sierra Nevada. \nSeveral inches of snow is possible above 7500 feet. Lighter \nrainfall spreads across the southern Great Basin and Mojave Desert\nlate Friday night and Saturday as the trough moves inland. Calmer\nweather arrives on Sunday as a transient shortwave ridge moves \nin. A stronger Pacific trough has potential to bring additional \nprecipitation, cooler temperatures, and increased winds Monday \ninto Tuesday. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Winds\nwill remain under 10 knots and generally follow typical, daily \npatterns. VFR conditions will persist through the TAF period.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Light winds below 10 \nknots anticipated over most of the region today, generally \nfollowing typical, daily patterns. The exception is the lower \nColorado River Valley (primarily KIFP to KEED) where speeds 8-14 \nknots and gusts around 20 knots are expected. These breezes will \nstay elevated tonight and into Wednesday. VFR conditions will \npersist through the TAF period\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Meltzer\nAVIATION...Stessman\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
